1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,565
Your phone
goes black.

2
00:00:01,565 --> 00:00:03,125
So does the sun.

3
00:00:03,125 --> 00:00:04,245
For five
seconds,

4
00:00:04,245 --> 00:00:05,755
there's no
light anywhere.

5
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,200
Then your phone
glows again.

6
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,920
The sky doesn't.

7
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,900
The sun is
shining,

8
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,580
but its light
needs over

9
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,920
eight minutes
to get here.

10
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:16,660
Until then,

11
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:18,220
noon looks
like midnight.

12
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,790
Not a single
star.

13
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,880
Right on time,

14
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:22,860
the sunlight
hits,

15
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:25,690
and the sky floods
back to blue.

16
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:29,000
That night, the
moon is back.

17
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,830
The stars
aren't.

18
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,480
Their light was
erased too.

19
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,820
The next closest is
four years away,

20
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,510
in the
southern sky.

21
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:41,440
Five seconds
of darkness.

22
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,480
Up north,

23
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,640
your first
star takes

24
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:45,310
nearly nine
years.
